## Level 2 completed

- `post-rpm-h-free-test-particle-action`: Explicit C² future-timelike curve and compact segment with fixed-endpoint variations; chain rule proves invariance for f′>0. The massive length action is adopted with m,c>0, not empirical evidence or a deduction from ideal-clock assumptions.
- `post-rpm-h-massless-shell-action`: Inverse metric and p-sharp are defined before use. Independent x,p,e variations precede imposing the nonzero future-null branch. Eliminating p yields (2e)^{-1}g(x′,x′), matching the separate massless einbein action; units agree and neither proper time nor mU is asserted.
- `thm-rpm-h-constraint-consistency`: Confirmed refuter:25:1: admissibility alone fails (χ=q, H_c=u=0, constant q=1). Added stationarity under explicit C² variations matching the exact supplier, applied to combined coordinates (q,p,u); its u equation is χ=0 and its q,p equations are Hamilton equations. Continuity includes endpoints. Differentiating χ gives consistency along the trajectory; tangency for all initial points is separately stated. Empty surfaces supply no stationary pair, r=0 recovers unconstrained dynamics, and no termination claim is made.
- `thm-rpm-h-first-class-local-reduction`: Independent dχ give r independent orthogonal fields; first-classness makes them tangent and r≤n. Closure makes the kernel involutive. Frobenius at constant rank gives coordinates; closure forces the dy-dy coefficients independent of s. Projection yields unique closed reduced form and the radical calculation proves nondegeneracy. r=0 and r=n are covered; no global Hausdorff assertion.
- `thm-rpm-h-local-legendre-and-energy-descent`: Fibre tangent has δt=δq=0 and Hessian·δv=0, so dE=0. Submersion fibres are manifolds; zero differential gives local constancy and connectedness gives constancy. Surjectivity defines unique h without choosing representatives; local sections prove smoothness with overlap agreement. Almost-regular hypotheses are assumed; no global velocity inverse is inferred.
- `thm-rpm-h-second-class-dirac-bracket`: Invertible skew C implies independent dχ and a regular level. Projected X_F^D annihilates dχ and contracts on TN to d(F|N). Invertibility removes the radical, closure pulls back, and the induced symplectic bracket has Jacobi and extension independence. Skew inverse fixes signs; χ substitution gives Casimir zero. Empty levels are vacuous and k=0 recovers the original bracket; singular C is excluded.

