## Level 3 completed

- `thm-rpm-h-flat-shell-global-reduction`: Future P0>0 makes the shell regular, excludes the null zero vertex, and provides a global inverse (y,a,p)→(yP0,a+yP,p). Characteristics translate y, so the quotient topology is exactly the open product projection onto B_m. Differentiating P0²=m²c²+|p|² cancels the dy terms, leaving da∧dp. Full flat lines meet any time slice once; no curved/global analogue is inferred.
- `thm-rpm-h-homogeneous-massive-shell`: With m,c,s>0 the derivative gives p=mc V-flat/s. The Hessian kills V and is positive on its Lorentz-orthogonal complement, so rank is three. Every future shell p has inverse representative V=p-sharp; all representatives are a connected positive ray. Vertical rank three plus four base directions gives rank seven onto the embedded regular shell. Zero energy follows from degree-one homogeneity; null/zero velocities are excluded.
- `thm-rpm-h-regular-local-gauge-slice`: The reader joint-zero hypothesis φ(z0)=χ(z0)=0 is essential and is now explicit. At z0 the block matrix with B=0 and invertible A is invertible and remains so on an ambient open neighborhood. Frobenius plus the inverse function theorem for (s,y)→(φ,y) gives one local intersection after shrinking to a product image. r=0 is explicit; no distant or returning global orbit intersection is ruled out.
- `cex-rpm-h-nonhausdorff-first-class-quotient`: dC=dp_x+a dp_y is nowhere zero; the single constraint is first class and its complete flow is ∂x+a∂y. The pigeonhole construction gives arbitrarily fine nets of irrational multiples, proving each fixed-momentum orbit dense. The two specified orbits are distinct by irrationality. A saturated nonempty open set meets that torus in the whole torus, preventing Hausdorff separation. No compactness of the total cotangent bundle is claimed.

## Level 4 completed

- `thm-rpm-h-first-order-action-and-geodesics`: Independent variations give all three shell equations; positive e and the selected nonzero future branch ensure regularity. The inverse-metric derivative and Christoffel formula yield ∇x′x′=(e′/e)x′. For m>0 auxiliary p,e have unique smooth values, and the chain rule cancels their stationary derivatives in both directions of action equivalence. dτ=em dλ gives e=1/m in proper time. For m=0 integrate dσ/dλ=e/e0>0; the transformed tangent has zero covariant acceleration, without proper time. Endpoint integration by parts is legitimate; no existence/completeness follows.

